<div class="wrap">
  <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <a href="/">Home</a><span class="sep">/</span><span>About</span>
  </nav>
</div>

<section class="hero" style="min-height:min(58vh,520px)">
  <div class="hero-bg">
    <img src="/img/photos/hero-wide.jpg" alt="Tea terraces" />
  </div>
  <div class="wrap hero-inner">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <span class="eyebrow">Since 2019</span>
      <h1 style="margin:16px 0 18px">A tea room, not a warehouse</h1>
      <p class="lede"><%= editorial.intro %></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="pillars">
      <% (editorial.pillars || []).forEach((p, i) => { %>
        <div class="pillar">
          <span class="num"><%= String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0') %></span>
          <h4><%= p.title %></h4>
          <p><%= p.body %></p>
        </div>
      <% }) %>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" style="border-top:1px solid var(--line-soft);background:var(--ink-850)">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="split">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">How we buy</span>
        <h2 style="margin:16px 0 22px">Three questions before a lot is listed</h2>
        <div class="stack-24" style="color:var(--text-dim);line-height:1.85">
          <p><strong class="gold">Where exactly was it grown?</strong> Not &ldquo;Fujian&rdquo; &mdash; the mountain. Altitude, soil and
            aspect change a tea more than any processing decision, and a grower who cannot tell you the mountain is
            usually a grower who bought the leaf from someone else.</p>
          <p><strong class="gold">When was it picked, and how was it fixed?</strong> For green and floral teas this is
            the whole game. A 2024 spring Longjing and a 2023 one are different products with the same name, and a
            hand-firing in a wok cannot be imitated by a machine.</p>
          <p><strong class="gold">Does it hold up across eight infusions?</strong> Cheap tea shows its faults on the
            second pour. Good tea gets more interesting. We brew every candidate gongfu-style, side by side with the
            lots we already sell, and we only list what wins.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="split-media">
        <img src="/img/photos/story-harvest-hero.jpg" alt="Tea being plucked" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap wrap-mid center">
    <span class="eyebrow">The practical bits</span>
    <h2 style="margin:16px 0 34px">Shipping &amp; payment</h2>
    <div class="grid grid-3" style="gap:30px;text-align:left">
      <div class="pillar">
        <h4>Shipped from Canada</h4>
        <p>Packed the same business day on orders before 2pm. Standard 2&ndash;5 business days domestically,
          7&ndash;14 internationally, tracked throughout.
          Complimentary over <%= money(store.freeShippingThreshold) %>.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pillar">
        <h4>Cards via OTT Pay</h4>
        <p>Visa, Mastercard, Amex, Discover, JCB, Diners and UnionPay, authenticated with 3-D Secure 2.
          Card data goes straight to the gateway &mdash; we keep only the brand and the last four digits.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pillar">
        <h4>If you do not like it</h4>
        <p>Unopened tins are returnable for 30 days, and if a tea simply is not to your taste we will replace
          or refund it without asking for the tin back. Tell us what you did like and we will suggest better.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section newsletter">
  <div class="wrap wrap-mid">
    <span class="eyebrow">Questions?</span>
    <h2 style="margin:16px 0 12px">Write to us</h2>
    <p class="muted" style="max-width:48ch;margin:0 auto 24px">
      Every email is answered by the person who chose the tea. Ask about a lot, a harvest, or what to buy for
      someone who thinks they dislike tea.
    </p>
    <a class="btn btn-solid" href="mailto:hello@chayuan.test">hello@chayuan.test</a>
  </div>
</section>
